Theorem TF-2a: Scalar PrimOp transfer produces SCALAR sentinel

  Preconditions:
    - Instruction is `Let { PrimOp(op, args) }` per Annex E §AIMS TF-2a
    - The typed primitive descriptor classifies `result = Scalar`
    - Descriptor arity equals `args.len`; every operand has an explicit
      Borrow or Consume use
    - `op` ranges over the scalar primitive operations enumerated in §3
      TF-2a + Appendix A row 3: integer arithmetic / float arithmetic /
      boolean / bitwise / comparison / shift kinds

  Soundness property:
    Forall typed PrimOp kinds op whose descriptor result is Scalar.
      transfer_tf2a(Let { PrimOp(op, _) }) = SCALAR
    AND L-6 layer (b) monotonicity holds for the constant function
    f(_) = SCALAR.

  Proof obligation:
    Two-part discharge:
      (a) Output enumeration — for each scalar PrimOp kind, the forward transfer
          rule per Appendix A row 3 emits `dst.state := SCALAR` on every
          per-dimension column (same shape as TF-1 row 1).
      (b) L-6 layer (b) monotonicity — TF-2a is a constant function:
          f(_) = SCALAR. Trivially monotone per the same argument as TF-1
          (constant functions preserve every partial order by L-4
          reflexivity on the constant codomain element).

    Part (a) — PrimOp kind enumeration (representative coverage of the
    primitive operation categories per Annex E §AIMS TF-2a):
      Integer arithmetic: IntAdd / IntSub / IntMul / IntDiv / IntRem
      Float arithmetic: FloatAdd / FloatMul
      Boolean: BoolAnd / BoolOr / BoolNot
      Bitwise: BitAnd / BitOr / BitXor / BitNot / Shl / Shr
      Comparison: IntEq / IntLt / FloatEq
      All 19 representative PrimOp kinds produce SCALAR per Appendix A row 3.
      Per Annex E §AIMS TF-2a + §1.8 L-9: these descriptor-classified
      outputs are scalar primitives outside the carrier-product domain;
      SCALAR applies regardless of arity or signedness. Heap-producing typed
      primitives are outside this quantifier and are governed by TF-2b.

    Part (b) — constant-function monotonicity:
      Identical argument to TF-1 Part (b): f(_) = SCALAR is constant;
      L-4 reflexivity gives SCALAR ≤ SCALAR; hence f(a) ≤ f(b) for any
      (a, b) in the input domain.

    Engines dispatched:
      monotonicity (PRIMARY — L-6 layer (b) per-rule discharge per
        section_04::verify_tf2a_primop_scalar — constant-function check)
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — Appendix A row 3 forward-transfer enumeration
        across 19 PrimOp kinds per section_04::verify_tf2a_primop_scalar)
      lattice (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully)
      refinement (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_04 monotonicity + case_analysis engines discharge TF-2a via 19 descriptor-classified scalar PrimOp kinds + constant-function monotonicity check
